      "content": "That's a good start on the general vibe, but it's a bit too \"fluff.\" Vance is a policy wonk; if he asks for the specifics on how 4b impacts the immediate bottom line for domestic manufacturers, this talking point won't hold water. \n\nThe memo clearly states that the compliance costs in this specific section will hit margins hard in Year 1. If he asks, \"Explain how this tax credit offsets the immediate rise in operational costs for these factories,\" what's our line? I need to know we aren't just ignoring the cost spike, but rather explaining it away as something beneficial or negligible.",
